    "result_text": "The full suite (the only test class, `AcceptanceTest`) passes with both tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` derived field on the owner API response, following the existing pattern for read-only computed fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `membershipNumber`).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipTier` property (enum `BRONZE`/`SILVER`) to the `Owner` schema. The `spring` openapi-generator produces `OwnerDto.MembershipTierEnum` and the JSON `membershipTier` field from this.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` for `membershipTier` backed by a new `formatMembershipTier` method that returns `SILVER` when `namesakeCount == 0` and a non-blank email is present, otherwise `BRONZE`.\n\nThe rule reuses the already-populated `namesakeCount` (set at creation in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`) and the owner's `email`, so it works on the `GET /api/owners/{id}` read path the tests exercise.\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest` (both `coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail` and `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail`) and the full `mvn test` build are green.",
